21649      data Children;
21650      input ID City$ @@;
21651      do i=1 to 4;
21652      input Age Smoke Symptom @@;
21653      output;
21654      end;
21655      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.CHILDREN has 100 observations and 6 variables.

21681      ;
21682      proc gee data=Children descending;
21683      class ID City;
21684      model Symptom = City Age Smoke / dist=bin link=logit;
21685      repeated subject=ID / type=exch covb corrw;
21686      run;

NOTE: PROC GEE is modeling the probability that Symptom='1'.
